& [Evidence] means an inspectable supported claim with provenance
  + evidence is not merely a value that can be serialized
  + evidence requires a subject, observation or derivation method, authority, lineage, and limits
  + a pure form can represent a claimed evidence grade without proving the claim is true
  + therefore InventoryConsistencyEvidence names the grade a future authorized issuer must substantiate

& [Consistency] is not selected as an unqualified state
  + consistency may describe agreement among observations
  + consistency must not silently become continuous world-state invariance
  + the old type name allowed both readings
  + the revised type explicitly resolves the ambiguity toward evidence grade

& [Inventory] means one complete ordered observation subject under one exact producer policy and scope
  + it is not a list of arbitrary caller values
  + complete is always relative to signed enumeration and resource rules
  + pure supplied assembly completeness is structural, not physical enumeration completeness

& [RepeatedInventory] means two actual inventory acquisitions
  + repetition is a physical and temporal relation
  + two copies of one value are not repetition
  + two caller-supplied carriers are not repetition without producer lineage
  + distinct correlation identities alone are not repetition
  + future acquisition lineage must establish actual production and order

& [Equal] means exact equality of committed canonical subjects under exact common scope
  + equality is assessed at the observation boundaries
  + equality does not state why subjects match
  + equality does not deny hidden collisions beyond ordinary digest assumptions
  + equality does not imply continuous sameness

& [NonAtomic] is a mandatory denial
  + no snapshot or transaction boundary
  + no tree-wide lock
  + no indivisible acquisition
  + no denial of interleaving
  + no denial of change-and-restore
  + no denial of post-observation change

& [Quiescent] is reserved
  + ordinary meaning is absence of relevant activity or change
  + two equal observations alone cannot prove that absence
  + supervisor-owned process accounting may narrow uncertainty but not eliminate external writers
  + no current variant uses quiescent

& [Stable] and [Unchanged] are reserved
  + both require a stated interval or transition relation
  + repeated equality supplies boundary observations but not uninterrupted interval proof
  + public API, faults, docs, evidence, and proof must not use them as aliases for the new grade

& [OsSnapshotProven] is a provenance-demanding reserved grade
  + OS identifies a platform primitive rather than generic software copying
  + Snapshot identifies an immutable or point-in-time subject according to that primitive
  + Proven requires exact primitive, issuer, identity, and binding evidence
  + enum presence does not satisfy those requirements
  + TopologyReceipt 0.3 therefore rejects it

& [Receipt] means a content-addressed claim envelope
  + pure TopologyReceipt validation checks schema and internal relations
  + a receipt is not authoritative merely because a caller constructs it
  + an issuer identity and proof are separate future obligations
  + consistency_evidence is one claim field inside the envelope

& [Producer] means an authority-bearing operation that creates evidence from observation
  + no producer is introduced here
  + a serializer is not a producer
  + a validator is not a producer
  + the digest reconciler is not an acquisition producer

& [Validator] means a pure syntax and relation checker
  + it may accept NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual as a coherent claimed grade
  + it cannot observe that two acquisitions occurred
  + it rejects OsSnapshotProven in the receipt because required relations cannot be represented

& [Profile] means exact machine-contract identity
  + machine meaning changes require profile changes
  + phase3 forms 0.2 identifies the new evidence vocabulary
  + topology forms 0.3 identifies the revised type use
  + receipt 0.3 identifies the renamed field and new allowed token
  + scanner 0.1 remains because physical behavior is untouched

& [Legacy] means a prior serialized contract, not malformed history
  + history remains valid evidence of what the prior system specified
  + revised decoders reject legacy input prospectively
  + rejection is not migration and does not rewrite history

& [ClauseRefinement_Actual] is exact
  + actual always modifies physical acquisition, not truth of caller claims
  + only later producer authority can establish actual

& [ClauseRefinement_Complete] is scoped
  + physical acquisition completeness depends on later signed traversal policy
  + pure carrier completeness does not upgrade it

& [ClauseRefinement_Ordered] is temporal only with acquisition provenance
  + left and right are not first and second
  + order requires explicit acquisition relation

& [ClauseRefinement_InitiallyPermitsOnly] is validator policy
  + TopologyReceipt 0.3 accepts only the weakest representable grade
  + it does not say every future scanner has already proven the grade

& [ClauseRefinement_Reserved] means named but unavailable for receipt success
  + reserved token supports a closed lattice without prematurely authorizing its use
  + a later profile may add provenance and permit it

& [InferenceRules] are closed
  + actual repeated acquisition plus exact scope plus complete first and second lineage plus Equal may support NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + supplied Equal alone cannot support it
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual cannot support Quiescent
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual cannot support OsSnapshotProven
  + form-valid receipt cannot support issuer authority
  + historical 0.2 receipt shape cannot support 0.3 meaning

& [AntiInferenceRules] are mandatory
  - never: infer actual from caller supplied
  - never: infer repeated from two values
  - never: infer temporal order from left and right
  - never: infer quiescent from equal
  - never: infer unchanged interval from equal boundaries
  - never: infer snapshot from double inventory
  - never: infer admission from receipt syntax
  - never: infer implementation authority from SJS intermediate

& [PublicVocabularyDisposition] is exact
  + accept InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + accept NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + accept non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + accept OsSnapshotProven only as reserved enum vocabulary
  + accept consistency_evidence
  + remove ConsistencyClass
  + remove QuiescentDoubleInventory
  + remove quiescent_double_inventory from current production Rust
  + remove consistency from current TopologyReceipt JSON

& [RefinementDecision] is passed
  + no source correction required
  + every ambiguous term has one selected meaning or explicit reservation
  + constraints and pruning remain separate next stages
  + implementation authority is absent
